# Scratch files the CPython test suite writes into the working directory.
# test/support/os_helper.py builds its name as "@test_<pid>_tmp", so the pid
# changes every run and a leaked one is a new path each time; test/support
# also uses the fixed "@grail_test_tmp".
@test_*_tmp
@grail_test_tmp
# CPython's XML test data includes an EXPECTED-OUTPUT file whose extension
# collides with the ``*.out'' build-output rule above.  It is vendored test
# INPUT, not something a run produces, and test_sax fails at import without it
# (findfile('test.xml.out')) -- so the whole data directory opts back in.
!src/python/stdlib/test/xmltestdata/
!src/python/stdlib/test/xmltestdata/*
